    "result_text": "All 16 tests pass, including the `AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsUnifiedMemberId` and the `FiscalYearTest`. The build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, and removed the derived `checkDigit` field.\n\n**New logic, placed where it belongs:**\n- **`util/MemberId.java`** (new) \u2014 owns the `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` format: `of(region, shortFiscalYear, hash8)` composes the body and appends the Luhn `CHK` over its digits (reusing the existing `LuhnCheckDigit`); `deduplicate(...)` handles collisions with a `-<n>` suffix; `regionOf(...)` reads the region back out by taking the leading letters (robust to the fiscal-year digits that follow and to any dedup suffix). This replaces the deleted `util/CustomerCode.java`.\n- **`rest/function/owner/AssignOwnerMemberId.java`** (new) \u2014 a single pipeline step that composes the region (`CityLocality`), fiscal year (`FiscalYear.shortYearOf`), `HASH8` (`Sha256` over normalized telephone + last name), builds the memberId and de-duplicates against existing ones. Replaces the two deleted steps `AssignOwnerCustomerCode` and `AssignOwnerMembershipNumber`.\n\n**Updated to reference `memberId`:**\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 field/column `member_id`, `getMemberId()/setMemberId()`; `getPrimaryIdentifier()` returns the memberId; `getLocality()` derives region via `MemberId.regionOf` (so `getOwnerSegment()` follows); removed the `customerCode`/`membershipNumber` accessors and `getCheckDigit()`.\n- **`AuditOwnerCreated`** and **`OwnerCreatedEvent`** \u2014 the human-readable audit line and the structured JSON event now carry `memberId`.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 the two assign steps collapsed into one `assignMemberId` step.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 replaced the `customerCode`, `checkDigit`, `membershipNumber` schema properties with a single `memberId` (drives the generated `OwnerDto`, auto-mapped by MapStruct); updated the `locality` description.\n- **DB schemas** (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres) \u2014 `owners` table now has `member_id`; `customer_code`/`membership_number` columns removed.\n\nThe FY value, audit record, and owner segment all now reference the memberId, and collision handling applies to it.",
